    <div>
      <h2>The vibe</h2>
      <p>On the shore of Lake Sainte-Croix, in Bauduen, this rental operator offers kayaks and paddleboards to explore the lake's turquoise waters, with the cliffs plunging into the water as a backdrop.</p>

      <h2>What to know before you go</h2>
      <p>It's explicitly confirmed: dogs are allowed on the paddleboards here, which remains a rarity on Lake Sainte-Croix, where many rental operators turn them away. A real plus if you want to enjoy the lake with your companion. One point of caution to note: on this type of inflatable gear, some rental operators on the lake exclude dogs (claws that could puncture the board) — a confirmation by phone before heading over is still recommended, even though this operator has been identified as accepting dogs.</p>
      <div class="callout">Coco's tip: call before coming to confirm availability and the conditions for your dog, especially in high season.</div>

      <h2>Nearby</h2>
      <p>Lake Sainte-Croix and the Verdon Gorges are right next door, to extend the outing on the water or on foot.</p>
